 *
 * This header is the single source of truth for the compile-time default of
 * the openuwb::timing instrumentation primitives.  Every translation unit
 * that includes <openuwb/support/timing.h> sees the SAME default, which keeps
 * the Enabled template parameter of the RAII scopes consistent between TUs
 * (ODR hazard), exactly like the ISA values in simd_config.h.
 *
 * UWB_TIMING_ENABLED_DEFAULT:
 *   1  the optional RAII scopes accumulate by default (the historical,
 *      always-on behaviour of the wall-clock stage boundaries)
 *   0  the RAII scopes compile empty by default; a TU can still opt in with
 *      ScopedNs<true>, so the option is a default, not a hard switch
 *
 * The plain (non-template) helpers -- elapsed_ns(), elapsed_us_since(),
 * elapsed_us_f(), thread_cpu_ns(), accumulate_ns() -- are never compiled out:
 * they are the measurement primitives, not instrumentation, and the existing
 * stage-boundary contracts (runner_summary.json, stdout console stats)
 * depend on them being present.
 */
#pragma once

#cmakedefine01 UWB_TIMING_ENABLED_DEFAULT
